<title>MEXICO: Mexico closes port on intense winds - gov't.</title>
<headline>Mexico closes port on intense winds - gov't.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Strong winds forced Campeche state port Ciudad del Carmen shut as of 1000 local/1600 GMT Wednesday, the communications and transportation ministry said in a meteorological update.</p>
<p>Crude oil shipping port Cayo Arcos, under the jurisdiction of Ciudad del Carmen, remained operating, port authority official Jose Manuel Ramon Garcia said.</p>
<p>Winds in the Gulf of Mexico and Yucatan peninsula reached up to 25 knots, with intense gusts expected to continue because of a cold front from the northeast U.S. coastline, the ministry said.</p>
<p>--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903</p>
